1 SAVE

   Writes the virtual VAX's ROM or NVRAM to a file, which LOAD reads
   back.  The qualifier that says which must be given.

   Format

     SAVE/ROM filespec
     SAVE/NVRAM filespec

   A plain SAVE, of a whole machine image, isn't in govax
   (%DCL-E-NEEDROMNVRAM).

2 Parameter

 filespec

   A host file, which is replaced if it's there.  (SAVE doesn't write
   volume files; COPY one there afterward.)

2 Description

   The file holds the image's first and last addresses, then each
   512-byte page that isn't all zeros, with its offset.

2 Qualifiers
/NVRAM

   Saves the NVRAM.

/ROM

   Saves the ROM.

2 Examples

   1.$ SAVE/ROM "current.rom"

     Writes the ROM to the host file current.rom.
